by stof at 2026-01-27T16:50:25Z

Reading a value from an array is `args['post']`, not `args.post`.

Unlike Twig where the dot operator is abstracting away the way to access a property, a getter or an array value, the ExpressionLanguage component has separate operators (due to the constraint of being able to compile the expression into a PHP expression with no runtime dependency on the component).
The `.` in ExpressionLanguage maps to the `->` operator in PHP, which is also not valid for PHP arrays.

