True, however, you could argue the same that `this.foo` in `new Assert\When('this.foo == "bar"')` in DTOs should also resolve private properties (which it doesn't).

> anything better other than this since this name cannot be used in the closure case

The names of closure arguments are not described within Symfony _(at least in the code)_, so not sure if huge issue.

The cache attribute exposes all controller arguments as top-level variables in EL evaluation, I'm a bit worried that using anything else than `this` may be already in use by someone's app/bundle logic. Because it's not possible to define `$this` as an argument for a method/function, it is guaranteed that no one is using it.

> It might be interesting to improve the EL component to make it able to run an expression with a scope set.

If we use `this` now, implementing this EL improvement later would mean we don't need to introduce any new variables / migrate from `self` to `this` etc.

